window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-horikita-suzune"]=[{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"classroom coercion  ch 2 opening  present late may  class 1 d classroom after final bell  ayanokoji is feigning sleep  sleeping strategy  pondering society  horikita approaches his desk and stands over him like an intimidating presence  described as a  devil  to shostakovich s symphony no  11   ayanokouji kun  do you have a moment   if you do not awaken within three seconds  i will bestow additional punishment upon you   see  you are awake after all  aren t you   glad to hear it  well then  may i have a little of your time   well  even though you have no right to veto such a decision  i suppose i would be exceptionally displeased   and when i am displeased  then i will prove a major obstacle to your school life  ayanokouji kun  for example  i might set a great number of thumbtacks on your chair  or  when you go to the toilet  i might splash water on you from above  or stab you with the needle of my mathematical compass  those kinds of obstacles  i suppose   don t worry  that was only a joke  i wouldn t splash water on you from above   after his harassment protest   evidence   she asked   what about the evidence  did you decide i m the culprit without evidence   demands proof when accused of previously stabbing his arm with a drawing compass   ayanokouji kun  would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair  which would you like more  because if you refuse me and force my hand  it will be your responsibility   all right  then  what am i supposed to do   ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom coercion (Ch.2 opening, present late May)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.16–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after final bell. Ayanokōji is feigning sleep (&quot;Sleeping Strategy&quot;) pondering society. Horikita approaches his desk and stands over him like an intimidating presence (described as a &quot;devil&quot; to Shostakovich&#x27;s Symphony No. 11).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun, do you have a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you do not awaken within three seconds, I will bestow additional punishment upon you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“See, you are awake after all, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Glad to hear it. Well then, may I have a little of your time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, even though you have no right to veto such a decision, I suppose I would be exceptionally displeased.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And when I am displeased, then I will prove a major obstacle to your school life, Ayanokouji-kun. For example, I might set a great number of thumbtacks on your chair. Or, when you go to the toilet, I might splash water on you from above. Or stab you with the needle of my mathematical compass. Those kinds of obstacles, I suppose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. That was only a joke. I wouldn’t splash water on you from above.” (after his harassment protest)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Evidence?” (she asked)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the evidence? Did you decide I’m the culprit without evidence?” (demands proof when accused of previously stabbing his arm with a drawing compass)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. Would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair? Which would you like more? Because if you refuse me and force my hand, it will be your responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “All right, then. What am I supposed to do?” (agrees under duress, filled with trepidation; the narrative then flashes back two months to the entrance ceremony — the favor itself is named only later, at p.150: “I need your help, Ayanokouji-kun.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Physical intimidation; stands directly over him; uses cold countdowns; completely denies physical violence (compass stab) on strict legalistic grounds (lack of evidence).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dominant, uncompromising, highly articulate, ruthlessly practical, utilizes psychological pressure and legalistic deflection.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Formal, polite yet chillingly authoritative diction (keigo combined with overt threats: &quot;bestow additional punishment&quot;, &quot;prove a major obstacle to your school life&quot;, &quot;regret while you suffer&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Master-slave / coerced partner dynamic; views him as someone she can leverage for assistance through relentless pressure; already comfortable threatening physical harm.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\">→ After: Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"entrance ceremony bus   rock gate confrontation  ch 2 flashback  april  crowded city bus heading to anhs on entrance ceremony day  an elderly woman stands shaking in the aisle  kushida appeals to passengers  koenji haughtily refuses to yield his priority seat  natural rock school gate outside anhs  as students disembark  horikita immediately intercepts ayanokoji before he enters   wait   calls out to him as he approaches the gate   you were looking at me  why   she asked  narrowing her eyes   that s right  i didn t consider giving it up  is there something wrong with that   you dislike trouble  then i don t think you and i are anything alike  i didn t give up my seat because i thought it would be pointless  that s all   perhaps  i m simply acting according to my own beliefs  that s different from someone who just dislikes trouble  like you  i don t want to spend any time around people like you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.20–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Crowded city bus heading to ANHS on entrance ceremony day. An elderly woman stands shaking in the aisle. Kushida appeals to passengers; Kōenji haughtily refuses to yield his priority seat. Natural rock school gate outside ANHS. As students disembark, Horikita immediately intercepts Ayanokōji before he enters.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait!” (calls out to him as he approaches the gate)<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You were looking at me. Why?” (she asked, narrowing her eyes)<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. I didn’t consider giving it up. Is there something wrong with that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits beside Ayanokōji near the elderly woman. Unlike the hesitant or ignoring passengers, she remains completely stone-faced and expressionless, completely immune to the surrounding emotional pressure.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Eyes lock with Ayanokōji across the aisle for an instant; shared silent mutual recognition that neither sees any reason to sacrifice their seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Confronts him directly; narrows her sharp eyes in suspicion.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You dislike trouble? Then I don’t think you and I are anything alike. I didn’t give up my seat because I thought it would be pointless. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps. I’m simply acting according to my own beliefs. That’s different from someone who just dislikes trouble, like you. I don’t want to spend any time around people like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Principle-driven individualism; fierce distinction between her rational convictions (&quot;pointless&quot;) and mere apathy (disliking trouble); openly hostile to people she deems weak-willed or apathetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Mutual dismissal; establishes deep boundary (&quot;don&#x27;t want to spend any time around people like you&quot;); walks off with identical mutual sigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p16-1\">← Before: Classroom coercion (Ch.2 opening, present late May)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\">→ After: Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"classroom day 1  assigned neighbors   favor exchange class 1 d classroom before ceremony  horikita sits down at the desk directly to ayanokoji s left  window column  rear   that s quite a heavy sigh  considering the school year has only begun  meeting you again makes me want to sigh   you just went ahead and introduced yourself   do you mind if i refuse   she asked  when he introduces himself   you re a curious one  aren t you  you won t find talking to me very interesting  though   replies when ak asks if she has friends in another class or enrolled alone   i m horikita suzune   introduces herself only after sighing and changing her mind   spoken just like someone who avoids trouble  i don t think i could ever like such a person   her verdict on ak s self description  adds  i pray this will be my only upset","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.27–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom before ceremony. Horikita sits down at the desk directly to Ayanokōji&#x27;s left (window column, rear).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s quite a heavy sigh, considering the school year has only begun. Meeting you again makes me want to sigh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You just went ahead and introduced yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you mind if I refuse?” (she asked, when he introduces himself)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re a curious one, aren’t you? You won’t find talking to me very interesting, though.” (replies when AK asks if she has friends in another class or enrolled alone)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita Suzune.” (introduces herself only after sighing and changing her mind)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Spoken just like someone who avoids trouble. I don’t think I could ever like such a person,” (her verdict on AK’s self-description; adds “I pray this will be my only upset.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deeply guarded and transactional; refuses engagement outright (“Do you mind if I refuse?”), performs self-introduction only under social pressure, and delivers a cutting verdict on AK’s “avoids trouble” persona; openly states she doesn’t want to spend time around people like him.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Clinical, dismissive boundary-setting; wraps rejection in pseudo-clinical judgments (“Spoken just like someone who avoids trouble”).<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Formally exchanges full names after visible reluctance; ends the exchange with mutual disdain (“I don’t want to spend any time around people like you” / “I feel the same way”).<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p20-1\">← Before: Entrance ceremony bus &amp; rock gate confrontation (Ch.2 flashback, April)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\">→ After: Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"rejection of hirata s introductions class 1 d classroom after chiyabashira leaves  hirata attempts class wide self introductions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom after Chiyabashira leaves. Hirata attempts class-wide self-introductions.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">When Sudō and others rebel and storm out, Horikita stands up from her desk without speaking a single word of introduction. She glances briefly at Ayanokōji, sees he isn&#x27;t moving, and walks straight out the classroom door…<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō and others rebel and storm out, Horikita stands up from her desk without speaking a single word of introduction. She glances briefly at Ayanokōji, sees he isn&#x27;t moving, and walks straight out the classroom door, completely unbothered by collective class harmony.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Utter disregard for peer pressure, social cohesion, or performative harmony.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p27-1\">← Before: Classroom Day 1: assigned neighbors &amp; favor exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\">→ After: Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"convenience store observation   pushover lecture campus convenience store on entrance afternoon  horikita stands reading a book in the aisle  dryly critiques ayanokoji s botched class introduction  notes his self introduction was painful to watch and achieved the exact opposite of making friends  berates ayanokoji for his submissive nature  tells him cleaning up another student s mess makes him look like a hopeless pushover and doormat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.41–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Campus convenience store on entrance afternoon. Horikita stands reading a book in the aisle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Dryly critiques Ayanokōji&#x27;s botched class introduction: notes his self-introduction was painful to watch and achieved the exact opposite of making friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Berates Ayanokōji for his submissive nature; tells him cleaning up another student&#x27;s mess makes him look like a hopeless pushover and doormat.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays quiet during Sudō&#x27;s altercation with the two mocking second-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Observes Ayanokōji stoop down and clean up Sudō&#x27;s spilled instant ramen cup from the floor outside the store.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Critical of passivity; views unrewarded, self-effacing kindness as weak and illogical.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Continued observation of his contradictory behavior; disdainful of his conflict-averse actions while remaining tethered to his vicinity.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p37-1\">← Before: Rejection of Hirata&#x27;s introductions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\">→ After: Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"lunchtime mockery of ayanokoji s isolation class 1 d classroom at lunch on day 2  ayanokoji is sitting alone  wishing someone would invite him to eat   how pathetic   i want someone to invite me along  i want to eat with someone  your thoughts are like an open book   that s right  i prefer to be alone  why don t you stop worrying about me and instead think about yourself   how tragic","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.54–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D classroom at lunch on Day 2. Ayanokōji is sitting alone, wishing someone would invite him to eat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“How pathetic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“‘I want someone to invite me along. I want to eat with someone!’ Your thoughts are like an open book.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s right. I prefer to be alone... Why don’t you stop worrying about me and instead think about yourself?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Laughs derisively at Ayanokōji from the adjacent desk.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Hirata invite the class to the cafeteria and get swarmed by girls (including Karuizawa Kei). Horikita scoffs at Ayanokōji&#x27;s outstretched, unreciprocated hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How tragic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives Ayanokōji one final pitying look before departing the classroom alone to eat in private.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fiercely defends solitude as a deliberate preference rather than a social defeat; observant of others&#x27; insecurities, uses sharp mockery as a defense mechanism.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p41-1\">← Before: Convenience store observation &amp; pushover lecture<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\">→ After: The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"the club fair invitation   the violence justification classroom 1 d afternoon lunch  ak returns with convenience store bread  later  walking to the gymnasium   i m not interested in joining a club   cuts ak off before he can even ask   ayanokouji kun  do you have dementia  or are you just an idiot  didn t i just tell you that i m not interested   you don t really have any friends  do you   she asked   listen  don t count me as one of your friends   you don t plan to join a club  but you want to go to the club fair  how odd  do you plan to use this as a pretext for talking to people and making friends   ayanokouji kun  i ve warned you thoroughly  but it would appear that you haven t been listening  i think i may have to dole out rather merciless punishment to you later   oh  really  violence has existed since the dawn of time  violence has historically proven to be the human race s most effective means of achieving resolution  violence is the most reliable method to make others listen  or safely deny their demands  not to mention that  in many countries  the police who enforce the law use handguns and batons  wielding violence as a tool to make arrests   well  if it s only for a little while after school  i ll go with you  she said   concedes to accompany him to the club fair strictly as an observer   watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.59–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D afternoon lunch (AK returns with convenience-store bread); later, walking to the gymnasium.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not interested in joining a club.” (cuts AK off before he can even ask)<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji-kun, do you have dementia, or are you just an idiot? Didn’t I just tell you that I’m not interested?”<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t really have any friends, do you?” (she asked)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Listen, don’t count me as one of your friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t plan to join a club, but you want to go to the club fair? How odd. Do you plan to use this as a pretext for talking to people and making friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Karate-chops Ayanokōji in the side when he presses her with a “mean-spirited” question, then delivers a grand speech justifying it: violence is the human race’s most effective means of resolution, older than recorded history, wielded even by police.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun. I’ve warned you thoroughly, but it would appear that you haven’t been listening. I think I may have to dole out rather merciless punishment to you later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, really? Violence has existed since the dawn of time. Violence has historically proven to be the human race’s most effective means of achieving resolution. Violence is the most reliable method to make others listen, or safely deny their demands. Not to mention that, in many countries, the police who enforce the law use handguns and batons, wielding violence as a tool to make arrests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if it’s only for a little while after school, I’ll go with you,” she said. (concedes to accompany him to the club fair strictly as an observer)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp-tongued and combative; justifies physical aggression with cold rationalization; concedes ground only when logic permits, framing every concession as her own limited choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Despite constant rejection, she repeatedly ends up accompanying him when reasoned with — on her terms only.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p54-1\">← Before: Lunchtime mockery of Ayanokōji&#x27;s isolation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\">→ After: The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune","q":"the student council president s speech  frozen shock gymnasium club fair  student council president horikita manabu takes the stage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.67–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium club fair. Student council president Horikita Manabu takes the stage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">As Manabu commands absolute silence across hundreds of students and delivers his stern manifesto against naive candidates, Suzune freezes completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Remains “still as a statue”, completely paralyzed; her eyes stay locked forward, and she gives no sign of hearing Ayanokōji speaking right next to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> While Ayanokōji is distracted exchanging contact info with Sudō, Ike, and Yamauchi, Suzune slips silently into the departing crowd and disappears alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Visceral, overwhelming psychological reaction to her brother&#x27;s presence; completely immobilizes her razor-sharp composure, reducing her to silence and flight.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p59-1\">← Before: The club-fair invitation &amp; the violence justification<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\">→ After: Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"friendship boundary   swimming performance classroom 1 d  morning before pe  then indoor swimming pool   from what i ve seen  you don t seem to be unsociable or lacking in communication skills  though   wait just a minute  i already warned you not to  but you wouldn t be thinking of me as your friend  would you   i see  i feel a little relieved","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.73–74, 78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D (morning before PE); then indoor swimming pool.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“From what I’ve seen, you don’t seem to be unsociable or lacking in communication skills, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait just a minute. I already warned you not to, but you wouldn’t be thinking of me as your friend, would you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. I feel a little relieved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at class and catches Ayanokōji eyeing the boys&#x27; group conversation. Scorns his hesitation (*&quot;Pathetic&quot;*).<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps backward in visible disgust when asking if he considers her a friend. When Ayanokōji replies that no matter how low he sinks he&#x27;d never dream of being her friend, she visibly relaxes.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Competes in the first girls&#x27; heat of 50m swimming; finishes in **approximately 28 seconds** with sharp, disciplined form.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Strong athletic competence; steadfast commitment to solitary status; deeply relieved when social boundaries are affirmed.<span class=\"pg\">p.73, 78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p67-1\">← Before: The Student Council President&#x27;s speech: frozen shock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\">→ After: Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"cafe trap unmasked   the ninth year alone classroom 1 d  then palate cafe in keyaki mall  palate cafe  ayanokoji invites her under the guise of thanking her for advice  seating them at a four person table and ordering a caramel latte  when kushida suddenly arrives pretending it is a coincidence  horikita dismantles the scheme instantly   not interested   don t invite me again  it s a bother   i don t like this  what are you plotting   icy look  the moment she sits down   i thought as much  i thought this whole thing was a little suspicious right from the start   also  we came straight here after classes ended  no matter how much those girls rushed  they could only have been here for about one to two minutes at the most  it was far too early for them to get up and leave  am i wrong   dismantles the timing of the  coincidental  encounter   i ve already said this many times  i want you to leave me alone  i have no intention of becoming friends with anyone in class  can you not understand that   to kushida  after  please be my friend   i wouldn t deny you your wish  but it s wrong to try forcing people into something against their will  being alone doesn t make me sad   besides  do you think that i would be happy if you forced me to become your friend  do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced   it s my fault for not being clear enough with you  so i don t blame you this time  but if you try this again  please keep in mind that i will not forgive you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.89–90, 94–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; then Palate Café in Keyaki Mall. Palate Café. Ayanokōji invites her under the guise of thanking her for advice, seating them at a four-person table and ordering a caramel latte. When Kushida suddenly arrives pretending it is a coincidence, Horikita dismantles the scheme instantly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Not interested.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t invite me again. It’s a bother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t like this. What are you plotting?” (icy look, the moment she sits down)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Packing textbook into her bag at the end of class. When Kushida approaches with a bright smile to invite her to a café, Horikita rejects her flatly without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Overhears other girls in the doorway whispering they hate her; remains completely indifferent.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Glares with razor-sharp deduction; exposes the setup before Kushida can even sit down.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought as much. I thought this whole thing was a little suspicious right from the start.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, we came straight here after classes ended. No matter how much those girls rushed, they could only have been here for about one to two minutes at the most. It was far too early for them to get up and leave. Am I wrong?” (dismantles the timing of the “coincidental” encounter)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already said this many times. I want you to leave me alone. I have no intention of becoming friends with anyone in class. Can you not understand that?” (to Kushida, after “Please be my friend!”)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wouldn’t deny you your wish, but it’s wrong to try forcing people into something against their will. Being alone doesn’t make me sad.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, do you think that I would be happy if you forced me to become your friend? Do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced?”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s my fault for not being clear enough with you, so I don’t blame you this time. But if you try this again, please keep in mind that I will not forgive you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes her untouched latte and stands up to leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Kushida murmurs that she feels they have met before, Horikita brutally cuts her off.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a waste of time. I find everything you’re saying unpleasant.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ayanokōji tries to mediate, warning her that spending three years without friends will be painful. Horikita nonchalantly drops a staggering revelation about her past.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It will be my ninth year in a row of being alone, so I’ll be fine. Oh, and if you include kindergarten, it would actually be slightly longer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida-san, if you don’t try to force me into anything, I won’t be rude. I promise. You’re not stupid, so you understand what I’m telling you, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives a cold, final parting and walks out into Keyaki Mall alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Total lifelong isolation: has lived without a single friend for over nine consecutive years (since elementary and kindergarten); solitary existence is her normal state.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Keen deductive perception: catches subtle environmental tells (table sizing, eye movements) instantly.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Utter refusal to entertain her overtures; finds her performative cheerfulness unpleasant; warns her against forced familiarity.<span class=\"pg\">p.89, 99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Catches him conspiring with Kushida; issues a firm, chilling warning that she will not forgive a second deception.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p73-1\">← Before: Friendship boundary &amp; swimming performance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\">→ After: The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"the s system shock   rejection of class cooperation classroom 1 d  morning homeroom on may 1st   wouldn t it be difficult to figure out those details at this stage  besides  i don t think you can resolve this simply by investigating  everyone in our class arrived late and talked too often   points are just a byproduct of our performance  though  not having points won t hinder our lives here at school  we have free options at almost every turn  right   while unfortunate  they ve simply reaped what they ve sown   i m sorry  can you ask someone else  i m not particularly good at discussing things with others   her first refusal   i m sorry  but i have no interest in something meaningless   i refuse  i won t participate   her words were stern  yet composed   final rejection   that s one perspective  yes  if we could easily solve this by talking  then that d be fine  however  if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion  the group will fall further into chaos  to the point where there s no hope of salvaging anything  besides  i can t meekly accept my current situation   post rejection rationale to ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.124–126, 132–136<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D. Morning homeroom on May 1st.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wouldn’t it be difficult to figure out those details at this stage? Besides, I don’t think you can resolve this simply by investigating. Everyone in our class arrived late and talked too often.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Points are just a byproduct of our performance, though. Not having points won’t hinder our lives here at school. We have free options at almost every turn, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“While unfortunate, they’ve simply reaped what they’ve sown.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Quietly tallies up the 98 absences/lates and 391 talking infractions in her notebook as Chabashira announces Class D&#x27;s conduct breakdown.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Correctly deduces the newly posted poster displays the evaluation results and point rankings across all four classes (A: 940, B: 650, C: 490, D: 0).<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Face stiffens in sheer disbelief and revolt when Chabashira announces Class D is sorted by incompetence and branded &quot;defective&quot; (corpus: &quot;You&#x27;re defective. This is just the result of you being defective.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Scores near the top of Class D on the diagnostic short test; held the 3rd highest entrance exam score among the entire first-year grade.<span class=\"pg\">p.128, 143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices Ayanokōji photographing the class point totals board with his phone and questions what he is doing; impatiently points out investigating infractions cannot undo the class&#x27;s established habit of talking and tardiness.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Hirata steps down from the podium and invites her and Ayanokōji to join a class cooperation discussion to raise points, Horikita shuts him down with icy disdain.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, can you ask someone else? I’m not particularly good at discussing things with others,” (her first refusal)<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I have no interest in something meaningless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse. I won’t participate.” (her words were stern, yet composed — final rejection)<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s one perspective, yes. If we could easily solve this by talking, then that’d be fine. However, if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion, the group will fall further into chaos, to the point where there’s no hope of salvaging anything. Besides, I can’t meekly accept my current situation.” (post-rejection rationale to Ayanokōji)<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Absolute meritocratic elitism; total contempt for collective failure; views social compromise as a toxic liability.<span class=\"pg\">p.133, 136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Rebuffs his leadership outright; views his idealistic consensus-building as weak and futile.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p89-1\">← Before: Café trap unmasked &amp; the ninth year alone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\">→ After: Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"faculty office protest   the all 50s revelation guidance office adjacent to faculty staff room   i will be frank  why was i sorted into class d   i solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination  i made no substantial mistakes on the interview  either  at the very least  i shouldn t have been sorted into class d   who could be happy with an incorrect evaluation  furthermore  the class rankings greatly impact our future prospects  of course i m dissatisfied   you still haven t given me an explanation  was i honestly sorted into class d  did anything go wrong with the grading  please double check   is that so  then i will ask the school again  at another time   i can t imagine it will be easy  though  forget overtaking class a  how in the world could those immature class d misfits gain more points  i can t see how it s possible   this is a rather frightening coincidence   why do you pretend not to know   what other reasons do you have","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.142–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Guidance office adjacent to faculty staff room.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I will be frank. Why was I sorted into Class D?”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination. I made no substantial mistakes on the interview, either. At the very least, I shouldn’t have been sorted into Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Who could be happy with an incorrect evaluation? Furthermore, the class rankings greatly impact our future prospects. Of course I’m dissatisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Marches into the faculty office over her placement in Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Marches into the faculty guidance office to directly confront Chabashira over her placement in Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Chabashira counters that common sense created Japan&#x27;s flawed hereditary succession and that academic ability alone does not define superiority, Horikita falters but refuses to concede.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still haven’t given me an explanation. Was I honestly sorted into Class D? Did anything go wrong with the grading? Please double-check.”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Then I will ask the school again, at another time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t imagine it will be easy, though. Forget overtaking Class A; how in the world could those immature Class D misfits gain more points? I can’t see how it’s possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gasps as Chabashira reveals Ayanokōji hiding in the kitchenette and produces his entrance examination answer sheets, showing exactly 50 out of 100 in Japanese, Math, English, Social Studies, and Science, plus 50 on the short test.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a rather frightening coincidence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flinches visibly when Chabashira points out AK solved a 3%-success-rate math problem with an advanced formula while botching a 76%-success problem, and warns her that AK may be more intelligent than she is.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you pretend not to know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What other reasons do you have?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Extreme academic pride; shaken to her core when confronted with an enigmatic peer who can manipulate test outcomes at will.<span class=\"pg\">p.143, 147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p124-1\">← Before: The S-System shock &amp; rejection of class cooperation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\">→ After: Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"stairwell confrontation   the pawn offer school corridor stairs   was your score really just a coincidence   i don t  but i also don t understand  ayanokouji kun  you said that you like to avoid trouble  but you don t seem to be interested in class a   when i entered this school  i thought graduation was my only goal  but the reality is different  i m not even at the starting line   no  you re right that no lone individual can solve this problem  we won t even make it to the starting line without everyone s help   we have three major  immediate issues  tardiness and talking during class are the first two  third  we must make sure no one fails the midterm exam   i need your help  ayanokouji kun   i always knew you d help  ayanokouji kun  i m grateful   no  i heard the voice inside your head  you said you d help   don t worry  i don t require your brain power  ayanokouji kun  leave the planning to me  and act as i tell you   unfortunately  no one else in class d is nearly as easy to manipulate as you   he s no good  even if he has some talent and ability  i can t use him  to use an analogy  think about the pieces in shogi  right now  i don t need a gold or silver general  i want a pawn   an interesting answer  but you don t seem like the type to make that effort  ayanokouji kun  besides  haven t you been thinking   i ve always been a pawn  i don t want to advance  all along   well  contact me once you ve given it some thought  i look forward to hearing from you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.148–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School corridor stairs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Was your score…really just a coincidence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t, but…I also don’t understand, Ayanokouji-kun. You said that you like to avoid trouble, but you don’t seem to be interested in Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When I entered this school, I thought graduation was my only goal. But the reality is different. I’m not even at the starting line.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows Ayanokōji out of the office and confronts him on the stairs, grilling him about his true motives.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Delivers a sharp karate chop to Ayanokōji&#x27;s ribs when he tells her not to act so proud.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. You’re right that no lone individual can solve this problem. We won’t even make it to the starting line without everyone’s help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have three major, immediate issues. Tardiness and talking during class are the first two. Third, we must make sure no one fails the midterm exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I need your help, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji flatly refuses (&quot;I refuse&quot;), she completely ignores him with unnerving composure.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I always knew you’d help, Ayanokouji-kun. I’m grateful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I heard the voice inside your head. You said you’d help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I don’t require your brain power, Ayanokouji-kun. Leave the planning to me, and act as I tell you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, no one else in Class D is nearly as easy to manipulate as you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji suggests she recruit Hirata instead, Horikita drops her iconic shogi metaphor, exposing her ruthless utilitarian mindset.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s no good. Even if he has some talent and ability, I can’t use him. To use an analogy, think about the pieces in shogi. Right now, I don’t need a gold or silver general. I want a pawn.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “An interesting answer, but you don’t seem like the type to make that effort, Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, haven’t you been thinking, ‘I’ve always been a pawn, I don’t want to advance,’ all along?”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, contact me once you’ve given it some thought. I look forward to hearing from you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Discovers his deliberate 50-point sandbagging; views him not as an equal partner or strategist, but as an easily disposable, obedient &quot;pawn&quot; to execute her directives while keeping his abilities hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p142-1\">← Before: Faculty office protest &amp; the all-50s revelation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"compass stabbing  cafeteria recruitment    kushida veto classroom 1 d  school cafeteria  dorm phone call   are you angry with me   what  when did i stab with you a compass needle  ayanokouji kun   so  just because i m holding something means i stabbed you   be careful  if you get caught sleeping  that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points   i don t quite understand the message you just sent me  not that part  the part about kushida  i didn t know about that   i don t remember giving you permission to do that  her grades aren t even failing   i don t like it  shouldn t you have sought my approval first   i understand  i suppose anything worth doing requires sacrifice  however  kushida may only help gather the students  she s not allowed to join the study group   i will not allow her into our study group  i refuse to budge on this   this has nothing to do with that  she didn t fail the test  inviting extra people will only mean more time spent and greater confusion   don t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152–157, 167–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classroom 1-D; school cafeteria; dorm phone call.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you angry with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What? When did I stab with you a compass needle, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, just because I’m holding something means I stabbed you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji begins nodding off in class before lunch, drives the sharp metal needle of her drawing compass directly into his right arm to wake him.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be careful. If you get caught sleeping, that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Invites Ayanokōji to lunch and treats him to an expensive cafeteria meal set to negotiate his assistance in gathering the failing students (Sudō, Ike, Yamauchi) for a midterm study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Ayanokōji late at night, furious upon learning he enlisted Kushida Kikyō to assemble the boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t quite understand the message you just sent me… Not that part. The part about Kushida. I didn’t know about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t remember giving you permission to do that. Her grades aren’t even failing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t like it. Shouldn’t you have sought my approval first?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. I suppose anything worth doing requires sacrifice. However, Kushida may only help gather the students. She’s not allowed to join the study group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will not allow her into our study group. I refuse to budge on this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This has nothing to do with that. She didn’t fail the test. Inviting extra people will only mean more time spent and greater confusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Abruptly hangs up the phone on Ayanokōji to avoid further compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p148-1\">← Before: Stairwell confrontation &amp; the pawn offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\">→ After: Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"library collapse    getting rid of dead weight  school library  after school   i m sorry  you re far too ignorant and incompetent   said by horikita  who d been silent until now   if you can t solve this problem  i seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring   you re right  this has nothing to do with me  your suffering won t influence me at all  i just pity you  you must have spent your whole life running from anything that presented a challenge   after sudo slams the desk   so  you lack the courage to hit me  don t use my gender as an excuse   i don t care if you get expelled  do what you want   interesting  didn t you come here because you can t study   i was certainly mistaken  even if i d helped them avoid failure this time  we would ve faced a similar dilemma soon after  we d have to go through this irritation all over again  eventually  they ll fail  i finally understand how unproductive this was  i don t have the time for it   i mean that it s better to get rid of the dead weight   even if that was how you truly felt  i wouldn t particularly care  but i don t think that you actually want to save them   i suppose you were the only one who understood me  ayanokouji kun  you re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots  if there s some subject you re struggling with  i could teach you   there s nothing to be gained from associating with people who ll likely be expelled soon   how incredibly selfish  you call them your friends  yet you simply ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.173–180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">School library, after school.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry, you’re far too ignorant and incompetent,” (said by Horikita, who’d been silent until now)<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you can’t solve this problem, I seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right. This has nothing to do with me. Your suffering won’t influence me at all. I just pity you. You must have spent your whole life running from anything that presented a challenge,” (after Sudō slams the desk)<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Arrives at the library with immaculate, meticulously organized study materials, but rigidly demands absolute silence, instantly suffocating the study group.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Mercilessly ridicules Sudō when he struggles with elementary fraction arithmetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudō slams the desk and threatens violence, she challenges him with unflinching, cold mockery.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you lack the courage to hit me? Don’t use my gender as an excuse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ike quits in protest against her condescension, Horikita shoots back with venomous indifference.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t care if you get expelled. Do what you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interesting. Didn’t you come here because you can’t study?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Formulates her cold, elitist conclusion as the boys walk out.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was certainly mistaken. Even if I’d helped them avoid failure this time, we would’ve faced a similar dilemma soon after. We’d have to go through this irritation all over again. Eventually, they’ll fail. I finally understand how unproductive this was. I don’t have the time for it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean that it’s better to get rid of the dead weight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Directly antagonizes Kushida, accusing her of faking her sympathy for the failing boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if that was how you truly felt, I wouldn’t particularly care. But I don’t think that you actually want to save them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Offers to tutor Ayanokōji alone in the empty library, calling him &quot;somewhat better than those worthless idiots,&quot; and calls AK cruel for passively watching his friends get expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose you were the only one who understood me, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots. If there’s some subject you’re struggling with, I could teach you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing to be gained from associating with people who’ll likely be expelled soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How incredibly selfish. You call them your friends, yet you simply stand by and watch as they’re expelled. From my point of view, you’re cruel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: Compass stabbing, cafeteria recruitment, &amp; Kushida veto<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\">→ After: Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"night assault by manabu  the equality debate    the devil s handshake pathway outside dormitories  late night   hmph  i m far different from the useless girl you once knew  niisan  i came here to catch you   that s  you re wrong about that  i ll show you  i ll reach class a right away  then   i i can t do that  i will definitely reach class a  i ll show you   niisan  i   a ayanokouji kun   stop it  ayanokouji kun   he s not my friend  just my classmate   i m going to drag myself up to class a even if it kills me   he s ranked fifth dan in karate and fourth dan in aikido   you also practice martial arts  don t you  ayanokouji kun  you must hold a dan rank   you purposefully get lower test scores  and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy  i really don t understand you   even if there are potential unknown negatives  it s better for the future of our class to abandon the failing students  wouldn t you regret not abandoning them when we do finally increase our points  right now  it s a risk that we should take   yes  really  i m at a complete loss as to why you re so desperate to save them   is that bad  people are calculating creatures  for the most part  if you sell goods  you receive money  if you do someone a favor  that debt of gratitude will be repaid  by giving up a seat  you gain the joy of contributing to society  am i wrong   who do you think you are  do you even have the ability to find fault with me   it s almost as if you re saying i m the same as sudou kun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.192–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pathway outside dormitories, late night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmph. I’m far different from the useless girl you once knew, niisan. I came here to catch you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s… You’re wrong about that. I’ll show you. I’ll reach Class A right away, then—”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I-I can’t do that… I will definitely reach Class A. I’ll show you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows her older brother Horikita Manabu into the darkness; completely paralyzed by fear and reverence. Submits powerlessly when he grabs her wrist and pins her against the concrete wall.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Niisan, I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gasps in strained shock as Ayanokōji physically intercepts her brother&#x27;s throw.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A-Ayanokouji-kun?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop it, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stunned by Ayanokōji evading her brother’s lethal strikes; denies to her brother that AK is her friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s…not my friend. Just my classmate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to drag myself up to Class A even if it kills me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sits slumped against the concrete wall in dejection; reveals Manabu’s formidable martial arts ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s ranked fifth dan in karate and fourth dan in aikido.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You also practice martial arts, don’t you, Ayanokouji-kun? You must hold a dan rank.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You purposefully get lower test scores, and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy. I really don’t understand you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Debates the nature of merit and human ability with Ayanokōji under the night sky. Defends absolute meritocracy.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if there are potential unknown negatives, it’s better for the future of our class to abandon the failing students. Wouldn’t you regret not abandoning them when we do finally increase our points? Right now, it’s a risk that we should take.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. Really. I’m at a complete loss as to why you’re so desperate to save them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that bad? People are calculating creatures, for the most part. If you sell goods, you receive money. If you do someone a favor, that debt of gratitude will be repaid. By giving up a seat, you gain the joy of contributing to society. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who do you think you are? Do you even have the ability to find fault with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stumbles when Ayanokōji diagnoses her fatal flaw: she isolates herself because she considers everyone else inferior baggage, blinding her to others&#x27; unique strengths (Sudō&#x27;s athletics, Ike&#x27;s communication) where she herself would drag down the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s almost as if you’re saying I’m the same as Sudou-kun and his group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is all pure conjecture. It’s nothing more than armchair speculation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Forced to concede the argument; shaken by Ayanokōji’s logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s frustrating, but what you said was basically correct. You’ve persuaded me; I have to concede that point. However, I still don’t understand you. What do you want? What is this school to you? Why did you work so hard to convince me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cut the crap. I want to know the real reason. Is it for points? To rise up, even by one class level? Or is it to save your friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Ayanokōji answers that he wants to understand true merit and equality, she extends her arm to seal an alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no way that you could fool me into believing you, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll look after Sudou-kun and the others, but for my own sake. I’ll make sure that they don’t get left behind, but only as a strategic means of securing an advantage for our future. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve come to an arrangement, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Devastating inferiority complex regarding her brother Manabu; fiercely stubborn yet fundamentally logical—can be persuaded by undeniable rational evidence; formalizes an explicit utilitarian pact with Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196, 202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Her primary psychological driver; desperate for his acknowledgment, but rendered completely docile and helpless in his presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Witnesses him deflect her brother’s lethal strikes; accepts his philosophical critique of her arrogance; seals the alliance (his narration: &quot;made a deal with the devil&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.194–202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p173-1\">← Before: Library collapse &amp; &quot;getting rid of dead weight&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\">→ After: The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"the reunion campaign  honesty   i hate you  and the in class study plan   here  look at this written contract   produces a ludicrous written contract making ak her workhorse until class a  he tears it up   no  this is for me   i m going to do it  definitely   declaring class a within earshot of kushida s doubts   fine  if everything goes well with the study group  i ll accept your help moving forward   conditionally admitting kushida into the wider class a project   i hate you  sudou kun   however  our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now  i will teach you for my own sake  you will do your best for your own sake  am i wrong   yes  exactly  otherwise  why would anyone willingly involve you   there are no shortcuts or cheap tricks when it comes to studying  you just have to spend your time carefully   turns his own basketball logic against him   put in the effort so that you can continue to play basketball at this school  don t throw away your own potential","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.203–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Here, look at this written contract.” (produces a ludicrous written contract making AK her workhorse until Class A; he tears it up)<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. This is for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m going to do it. Definitely,” (declaring Class A within earshot of Kushida&#x27;s doubts)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> One and a half months in: smacks Ayanokōji awake mid-thought, checks him for fever, and dispatches him to re-recruit the fallen study group — while grumbling that &quot;Sacrifices are inevitable&quot; over needing Kushida again.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Personally invites Kushida to lunch at Palate and treats her to a drink — the site of her earlier fury — then answers Kushida&#x27;s motive probe with total honesty.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fine. If everything goes well with the study group, I’ll accept your help moving forward,” (conditionally admitting Kushida into the wider Class A project)<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When Sudou demands a sincere apology for the library insults, refuses point-blank — then detonates the opposite move.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hate you, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now. I will teach you for my own sake. You will do your best for your own sake. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, exactly. Otherwise, why would anyone willingly involve you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Unveils her notebook schedule: exploit the six wasted hours of class time instead of scarce after-school hours; AK/Kushida/Horikita each tutor one-on-one in ten-minute breaks; memorize, don&#x27;t take notes.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are no shortcuts or cheap tricks when it comes to studying. You just have to spend your time carefully.” (turns his own basketball logic against him)<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Put in the effort so that you can continue to play basketball at this school. Don’t throw away your own potential.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts Ayanokōji&#x27;s manufactured date-stakes incentive as her own: &quot;boys are the simplest creatures on earth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Practical honesty as a weapon (confesses selfish motives to win Kushida); refuses performative apology; engineering instinct — restructures time itself rather than demanding willpower.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Major compromise: tolerates Kushida&#x27;s proximity for capability, granting conditional entry to the Class A project.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p192-1\">← Before: Night assault by Manabu, the equality debate, &amp; the devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\">→ After: The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"the hate confirmation   the basketball apology   really  thank you for everything you ve done  if you weren t here  the study group would not have succeeded   you hate me  don t you   you re not answering my question because it s true  right   no  that s unnecessary  knowing that is good enough  i can continue working with you without hesitation   hearing  i really hate you  changes nothing   pure utility logic   pervert   sudou kun  memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers   it was certainly your fault for not reviewing the old test s final section  however  as you said  you did everything that you could with the time that you had  you didn t cut any corners or give up  considering how much effort you put in  i think you should hold your head high and feel proud   comfort  i m speaking the truth  when i look at how far you ve come  i understand how hard studying is for you  sudou   i never thought i needed to understand anyone except for myself  so when you first told me that you wanted to play basketball  i insulted you  however  i now regret that  someone who doesn t understand how difficult  how arduous basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish   sudou kun  don t forget the hard work and effort that you poured into studying  apply that diligence to basketball  if you do  you might be able to go pro  at least  that s how i feel   i m sorry for what i said back then  well  now that i ve said my piece  i ll be","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.237–245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Really, thank you for everything you’ve done. If you weren’t here, the study group would not have succeeded.”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You hate me, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re not answering my question because it’s true. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Gives Kushida genuine, unprompted praise for the old-test distribution — including precise analysis of why announcing it after class protected everyone&#x27;s motivation.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stops Kushida at the door for the one confirmation she needs before trusting the partnership.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. That’s unnecessary. Knowing that is good enough. I can continue working with you without hesitation.” (hearing &quot;I really hate you&quot; changes nothing — pure utility logic)<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Glances at Ayanokōji and shuts down his swimsuit-daydream with one word.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Pervert.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> During the break, leaps to Sudou&#x27;s side and triages his ten-minute English crisis with tactical advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Steps in front of sulking Sudou after the exam and delivers her first genuine encouragement.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was certainly your fault for not reviewing the old test’s final section. However, as you said, you did everything that you could with the time that you had. You didn’t cut any corners or give up. Considering how much effort you put in, I think you should hold your head high and feel proud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Comfort? I’m speaking the truth. When I look at how far you’ve come, I understand how hard studying is for you, Sudou.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Amends her earlier scorn for his professional-basketball dream — having researched the actual career path — and bows her head in a formal apology.<span class=\"pg\">p.244–245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never thought I needed to understand anyone except for myself. So when you first told me that you wanted to play basketball, I insulted you. However, I now regret that. Someone who doesn’t understand how difficult, how arduous basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun, don’t forget the hard work and effort that you poured into studying. Apply that diligence to basketball. If you do, you might be able to go pro. At least, that’s how I feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry for what I said back then. Well. Now that I’ve said my piece, I’ll be going.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Growth arc: converts hate into explicitly acknowledged working distrust; capable of researched, bow-level apology when her earlier judgment is proven wrong — delivered in her usual aloof manner but unmistakable.<span class=\"pg\">p.238, 244–245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Trusts utility over affection: proceeds &quot;without hesitation&quot; on a confirmed mutual hatred.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> From library tormentor to coach and apologizer — the pivot that fully wins his loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.241, 244–245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p203-1\">← Before: The reunion campaign: honesty, &quot;I hate you,&quot; and the in-class study plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\">→ After: The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"the 51 point sacrifice    defective  not trash    earlier  you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty two points  you arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today  were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test   avg 64 4   2   32 2   they set 32  decimal dropped   inconsistency trap   i m sorry  i should have tried to lower my score just a little more   don t misunderstand  i did this for my own sake  it was all for nothing  though   to sudou s  you said that you hated me   i ll pay  too   joining her id card to ak s for the 100 000 point purchase   i wonder  when i look at him  all i see is a disagreeable student   answering chabashira s talent question   lists his deliberate low scores  stolen credit  and test point purchase   i don t know about him  but i most definitely will   on reaching higher classes   honestly  maybe the students in class d are defective  however  that doesn t mean they re trash   the difference is paper thin  however  with repairs  a defective product may become a superior article","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.249–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Earlier, you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty-two points. You arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today. Were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test?”…”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. I should have tried to lower my score just a little more,”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t misunderstand. I did this for my own sake. It was all for nothing, though.” (to Sudou&#x27;s &quot;You said that you hated me&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Breaks her lifelong pattern: raises her hand and speaks voluntarily for the first time all year, shocking Chabashira and the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Earlier, you said that the previous test had a passing grade of thirty-two points. You arrived at that number by the same formula you showed us today. Were there no mistakes in calculating the passing grade for the last test?” (avg 64.4 ÷ 2 = 32.2 → they set 32: decimal dropped — inconsistency trap)<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The class realizes the truth: she scored **perfect in four subjects but deliberately botched English to 51** — dragging the English average down so Sudou&#x27;s 39 would clear the threshold.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After Chabashira&#x27;s rounding kill destroys the counter-argument, mutters her apology to Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Appears behind Ayanokōji in the faculty-room hallway and backs the point-buying play without a second&#x27;s hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll pay, too,” (joining her ID card to AK&#x27;s for the 100,000-point purchase)<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder. When I look at him, all I see is a disagreeable student.” (answering Chabashira&#x27;s talent question — lists his deliberate low scores, stolen credit, and test-point purchase)<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know about him, but I most definitely will.” (on reaching higher classes)<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Returns Chabashira&#x27;s gaze and delivers her transformed class philosophy.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, maybe the students in Class D are defective. However, that doesn’t mean they’re trash.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The difference is paper thin. However, with repairs, a defective product may become a superior article.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Chops Ayanokōji in the side as they return — &quot;For whatever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Willing to burn her own exam score for a student who hates her (utility-framed as self-interest); publicly redefines her class from baggage to repairable material — the transformation Chabashira visibly registers.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Secretly gambles her English grade to save him; frames it as &quot;for my own sake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Bests her once (forcing the rounding confession), loses the round, then wins her approval with the trash/repairs answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.249, 254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Wordlessly joins the 100,000-point risk — the pact operating in practice.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p237-1\">← Before: The hate confirmation &amp; the basketball apology<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: The victory party: attending, deflecting, enlisting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"the victory party  attending  deflecting  enlisting   i did it for my own sake  if someone had been expelled  class d s evaluation would ve worsened   her answer to the party s thanks   it d be fine with me if you didn t   rejecting ike s plea to just pretend she cares   hmm  i don t really remember   our next challenge is the final exam  we should expect those questions to be even more difficult than the ones today  in addition  we still need to find a way to increase our points   drags celebration back to strategy   did you not see class d s average score  we were the lowest of all of the classes by far  if you think that we ll get points for that  then i think you need to open your eyes   i think you should learn to live a more modest life and give up on points   studying isn t the sole factor in deciding who goes into what class  though  right   planting the non academic path   i guess if you combined all three of their test scores  you d get one normal person s grade   systematically knocking down every morale boost kushida builds   i never wanted your help  sudou kun  besides  i have a hard time imagining how you ll be useful in the first place   thank you  i appreciate your words of praise   to sudou s  you re a really annoying girl   in this school  ability is paramount  i m positive that our competition will grow even more severe moving forward  if you say you ll work with us  know that you can t do so half heartedly  otherwise you ll be a burden   i really can t exp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The victory party: attending, deflecting, enlisting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256–262<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I did it for my own sake. If someone had been expelled, Class D’s evaluation would’ve worsened.” (her answer to the party&#x27;s thanks)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’d be fine with me if you didn’t.” (rejecting Ike&#x27;s plea to just pretend she cares)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm, I don’t really remember.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Attends the celebration in Ayanokōji&#x27;s dorm room — sitting outside the circle, quietly reading a novel; narration flags her mere presence as progress the old Horikita would never have allowed.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the party asks how the expulsion was reversed, plays total ignorance — preserving the point-purchase secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our next challenge is the final exam. We should expect those questions to be even more difficult than the ones today. In addition, we still need to find a way to increase our points.” (drags celebration back to strategy)<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you not see Class D’s average score? We were the lowest of all of the classes by far. If you think that we’ll get points for that, then I think you need to open your eyes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think you should learn to live a more modest life and give up on points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Studying isn’t the sole factor in deciding who goes into what class, though. Right?” (planting the non-academic path)<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess if you combined all three of their test scores, you’d get one normal person’s grade.” (systematically knocking down every morale boost Kushida builds)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never wanted your help, Sudou-kun. Besides, I have a hard time imagining how you’ll be useful in the first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. I appreciate your words of praise.” (to Sudou&#x27;s &quot;You&#x27;re a really annoying girl&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In this school, ability is paramount. I’m positive that our competition will grow even more severe moving forward. If you say you’ll work with us, know that you can’t do so half-heartedly. Otherwise you’ll be a burden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really can’t expect anything from you at all.” (to Sudou&#x27;s physical-ability volunteering)<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Progress without softening: attends, jokes-in-her-own-way, guards the secret, and converts a party into a war council — her will to Class A declared unshakeable.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–262<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v1-p249-1\">← Before: The 51-point sacrifice &amp; &quot;defective, not trash&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 1  july 1  reading the point board correctly   this isn t good  could they have figured out a way to increase their point total   it s too early to celebrate  all the other classes saw a similar increase in their points  we didn t close the distance at all  this might just be a reward first year students receive for getting through the midterm  every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points   so that s what happened  i thought it odd that we d been awarded points so quickly   no  that s not it  we managed to get something this time  after all   to ak s jab about the widening gap  then falls silent  refusing to explain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This isn’t good. Could they have figured out a way to increase their point total?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class…<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So that’s what happened. I thought it odd that we’d been awarded points so quickly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, that’s not it. We managed to get something this time, after all.&quot; (to AK&#x27;s jab about the widening gap; then falls silent, refusing to explain)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Only student tracking other classes&#x27; totals; celebration-proof — measures relative gap, not absolute gain.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  lunch  the bento era   you re still not used to it  you re as pathetic as ever  ayanokouji kun   noticing him scanning for lunch invitations   i m quite fine  thank you   his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally   i m not sure about that  the school supermarket provides free ingredients  you know   anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the internet  our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools  as well   the cafeteria is noisy  it s much more relaxing to eat here  wouldn t you say   you re always staring out at the ocean  but you don t have a surfboard  you lack even the determination to ride the wave  don t you  and you talk about missing it  you re awfully full of yourself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19–21<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’re still not used to it. You’re as pathetic as ever, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; (noticing him scanning for lunch invitations)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m quite fine, thank you.&quot; (his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally)<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not sure about that. The school supermarket provides free ingredients, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the Internet. Our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools, as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The cafeteria is noisy. It’s much more relaxing to eat here, wouldn’t you say?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re always staring out at the ocean, but you don’t have a surfboard. You lack even the determination to ride the wave, don’t you? And you talk about missing it? You’re awfully full of yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> New budget coping routine: home-made bento from free supermarket ingredients; refuses the free-cafeteria-subsidy optics; roasts AK with ocean/surfboard metaphor unprompted.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 3  after school  points paranoia  chat refusal  oil and water   do you think so  too  that it would have been better if sudou kun were expelled   opening  while packing every textbook   hmm  well  we still don t know whether our points would go up as a class  really   on her own midterm rescue of sudou   feigned disinterest   i m a little worried about what chabashira sensei said this morning   yes  she said that there was trouble  but did she mean that it was a problem for the school  or a problem for us  the students  if it s the latter  then   i hope that s the case  trouble directly affects our points   i m not interested in the slightest  also  i keep my notifications turned off   class group chat  joined but zero participation  keeps the app so leaving won t notify kushida   you ve been quite talkative lately  ayanokouji kun   it s a slight difference  but you ve changed   did something make you change   you seem to be getting along quite well with kushida san  aren t you bothered  especially knowing about her other side   hmm  well  you may have a point there  it s true that i hate you  too  ayanokouji kun  yet i talk to you normally  i don t really mind  then   that s what i m getting at  if someone says that they hate another person  it s fine  but if someone says that they hate you  don t you feel a little bad   i don t have any intention of getting in her way  but kushida san and i are like oil and water  i think it s better not to associate with her   who ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you think so, too? That it would have been better if Sudou-kun were expelled?&quot; (opening, while packing every textbook)<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hmm. Well, we still don’t know whether our points would go up as a class, really,&quot; (on her own midterm rescue of Sudou — feigned disinterest)<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m a little worried about what Chabashira-sensei said this morning,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes. She said that there was trouble, but did she mean that it was a problem for the school, or a problem for us, the students? If it’s the latter, then…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I hope that’s the case. Trouble directly affects our points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not interested in the slightest. Also, I keep my notifications turned off.&quot; (class group chat: joined but zero participation; keeps the app so leaving won&#x27;t notify Kushida)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’ve been quite talkative lately, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s a slight difference, but you’ve changed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did something make you change?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You seem to be getting along quite well with Kushida-san. Aren’t you bothered, especially knowing about her other side?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm. Well, you may have a point there. It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally. I don’t really mind, then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s what I’m getting at. If someone says that they hate another person, it’s fine. But if someone says that they hate you, don’t you feel a little bad?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t have any intention of getting in her way, but Kushida-san and I are like oil and water. I think it’s better not to associate with her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who knows? She probably doesn’t know that much about me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you’re that curious, why don’t you ask her yourself? Directly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What you just said was really disgusting, you know that?&quot; (reaction to &quot;I&#x27;m fine with the Kushida we have now&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs the worst-case simulation on every institutional signal; her hate lines are delivered analytically, then re-used as a lesson about honesty; deliberate testing of AK (his: &quot;Were you testing me?&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Daily walk-back ritual; she monitors his behavioral drift and says so; conversation register now includes open hostility-as-rapport (&quot;It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Declares them &quot;like oil and water&quot;; refuses any shared-group engagement with her; genuinely does not know Kushida&#x27;s rooftop face.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Won&#x27;t call for his expulsion yet discounts defending him publicly; frames everything through class-point consequences.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 1  cafeteria  refusing sudou in front of the group she takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria  ak watches her  looking slightly irritated  while the group tries to work out her reasons without her   you seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again  sudou kun   sorry  but i don t feel like helping you this time   for class d to rise through the ranks  it s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible  however  we probably won t get any points now  thanks to you  you hindered those plans   you keep focusing on who started the fight  but that s a trivial detail  did you never consider that   is that so  well  best of luck to you   don t make me laugh  i ve never once considered you a friend  nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn t recognize his own stupidity  goodbye   what idea  to toss me out like the trash   sudou throwing her refusal back at ak","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria; AK watches her &quot;looking slightly irritated&quot; while the group tries to work out her reasons without her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry, but I don’t feel like helping you this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“For Class D to rise through the ranks, it’s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible. However, we probably won’t get any points now, thanks to you. You hindered those plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You keep focusing on who started the fight, but that’s a trivial detail. Did you never consider that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Well, best of luck to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t make me laugh. I’ve never once considered you a friend. Nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn’t recognize his own stupidity. Goodbye.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The refusal is delivered as arithmetic, not malice: &quot;Horikita appeared more exasperated than angry. She let out a deep sigh, and left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What idea? To toss me out like the trash?” (Sudou throwing her refusal back at AK)<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 2  walked out on  chased down  and still not moved announces  all right  i m going to the dorms  nods  without hesitation  and leaves  she  didn t quail under everyone s gazes  which all expressed variations on  you re leaving   what is it   i thought i already declined  a few minutes ago  no less   you re free to run about for sudou kun s sake  i ve no right to stop you  however  if you need help  try someone else  i m busy   i have an important daily routine  so i need my alone time  it s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me   even if i step in and save him now  he ll land himself in trouble again  it s a vicious cycle  isn t it  you seem to think that sudou kun is the victim here  but i think differently   maybe the class c students really did start this fight  but sudou kun was also one of the perpetrators   why was he dragged into the fight  this problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question  got it  i do not wish to help until that question is answered  since you weren t able to convince me  why don t you ask the guy standing next to you  even though he pretends not to understand what i m thinking  he probably does","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces &quot;All right, I’m going to the dorms,&quot; nods &quot;without hesitation&quot; and leaves; she &quot;didn’t quail under everyone’s gazes, which all expressed variations on &#x27;You’re leaving?&#x27;&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought I already declined? A few minutes ago, no less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re free to run about for Sudou-kun’s sake. I’ve no right to stop you. However, if you need help, try someone else. I’m busy,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s portrait of the manner: &quot;She would probably grow up to be a fierce woman, the type that leaves social outings without reading the room and concludes meetings exactly on time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have an important daily routine, so I need my alone time. It’s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I step in and save him now, he’ll land himself in trouble again. It’s a vicious cycle, isn’t it? You seem to think that Sudou-kun is the victim here, but I think differently.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe the Class C students really did start this fight, but Sudou-kun was also one of the perpetrators.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why was he dragged into the fight? This problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question. Got it? I do not wish to help until that question is answered. Since you weren’t able to convince me, why don’t you ask the guy standing next to you? Even though he pretends not to understand what I’m thinking, he probably does.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s &quot;necessary to reach Class A&quot; argument bounces off her because she is not arguing about points: she sets a precondition (explain why the fight happened) that no one in the class is willing to meet, then walks.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> In front of Kushida she claims AK reads her mind — the first time the private shorthand between them is asserted to a third party. AK&#x27;s reaction is refusal: &quot;Please stop saying that I understand you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s gloss on her motive, said only in his own head: &quot;Horikita wasn’t the type to teach through kindness. She didn’t feel an obligation to others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 0  the class change question  and a point based reason to save sudou her reading material while the class argues about points   horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading  almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise  at a glance  i saw she was reading dostoevsky s demons  chabashira s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first   horikita looked up from her book  probably trying to gauge whether chabashira sensei was lying  she drops the subject the moment the answer arrives   horikita returned to reading  likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all   may i ask one question  please    ak   the watchful horikita raised her hand  she looked quite determined  considering this was a potential road to class a   what is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school  i m just asking for the sake of reference   so  you re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods  12 million points is about the limit    ak s tag   horikita muttered   we should save him because he s in a club    her first question back to ak s argument that sudou has point value   i have a hard time imagining that he d use his points altruistically  though   i won t say that i ll help  but i suppose i ought to acknowledge sudou s existence  at least a little    the movement ak gets out of her in this chapter  stated as little as possible   horikita s language was harsh  but she acknowledged the","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.67–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her reading material while the class argues about points: &quot;Horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading, almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise. At a glance, I saw she was reading Dostoevsky’s Demons.&quot; Chabashira&#x27;s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first: &quot;Horikita looked up from her book, probably trying to gauge whether Chabashira-sensei was lying.&quot; She drops the subject the moment the answer arrives: &quot;Horikita returned to reading, likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;May I ask one question, please?&quot; — AK: &quot;The watchful Horikita raised her hand. She looked quite determined, considering this was a potential road to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school? I’m just asking for the sake of reference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So, you’re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods, 12 million points is about the limit?&quot; — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Horikita muttered.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is the only student in the room who reacts to the class&#x27;s griping with contempt, and AK is the only one who sees it: &quot;Horikita spontaneously broke into derisive laughter in response to Ike and Karuizawa’s delusions. As her neighbor, I was the only one who noticed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should save him because he’s in a club?&quot; — her first question back to AK&#x27;s argument that Sudou has point value.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a hard time imagining that he’d use his points altruistically, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won’t say that I’ll help, but I suppose I ought to acknowledge Sudou’s existence, at least a little.&quot; — the movement AK gets out of her in this chapter, stated as little as possible: &quot;Horikita’s language was harsh, but she acknowledged the connection to her own interests.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the school for data, not for sympathy: the only two questions she volunteers in the chapter are about the maximum points ever saved and whether the rule is a lie — and she stops arguing the moment the arithmetic says no.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Chabashira&#x27;s claim that a class can be bought is verified by exactly two people in the room, and the teacher&#x27;s glance names them: &quot;Chabashira-sensei shot a quick glance over at Horikita and me. We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 1  she names the witness  and refuses the credit she appears at ak s door unannounced  the first time in the volume she seeks him out   just then  my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared  while i considered who this new visitor might be  she peered through the door   have you made any progress finding the witness    ak   asked horikita  looking as if she already knew the response   i m only telling you this because it s you  but i may have found out something    she stops mid sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave  kushida s wave forces her in   i didn t particularly plan on helping  you don t appear to have found the witness yet  right  her verdict on kushida s plan  given without being asked to join it   i wouldn t say it s a bad plan  provided you have sufficient time  your labors may actually bear fruit   i ll give you just one piece of advice  to help your pathetic odds    then the advice itself   it s hard to see what s right in front of you  if someone actually witnessed sudou s incident  then that person is close by   sakura san    then  on being pressed   she s the witness  she saw the incident  the whole method  in one answer   when kushida san said that she was looking for a witness in class  sakura looked down  a lot of students were staring at kushida san  sakura was the only one who didn t appear interested  she wouldn t have acted that way without some connection to the incident   no  sakura san is undoubtedly the witness  her actions c","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.75–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She appears at AK&#x27;s door unannounced, the first time in the volume she seeks him out: &quot;Just then, my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared... While I considered who this new visitor might be, she peered through the door.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Have you made any progress finding the witness?&quot; — AK: &quot;asked Horikita, looking as if she already knew the response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m only telling you this because it’s you, but I may have found out something—&quot; — she stops mid-sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave; Kushida&#x27;s wave forces her in.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn’t particularly plan on helping. You don’t appear to have found the witness yet, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on Kushida&#x27;s plan, given without being asked to join it: &quot;I wouldn’t say it’s a bad plan. Provided you have sufficient time, your labors may actually bear fruit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll give you just one piece of advice, to help your pathetic odds,&quot; — then the advice itself: &quot;It’s hard to see what’s right in front of you. If someone actually witnessed Sudou’s incident, then that person is close by.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san.&quot; — then, on being pressed: &quot;She’s the witness. She saw the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The whole method, in one answer: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who didn’t appear interested. She wouldn’t have acted that way without some connection to the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s measure of what she did: &quot;I hadn’t noticed that at all. I was genuinely impressed by Horikita’s observational prowess. She’d noticed a classmate’s very minor gesture.&quot; — and his summary of the chapter&#x27;s turn: &quot;While we’d been paralyzed by uncertainty, Horikita had stepped up and taken control.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, Sakura-san is undoubtedly the witness. Her actions confirmed it. Although she may not admit to it, she is definitely the one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She rejects the rescue narrative outright: &quot;Don’t misunderstand. I just didn’t want to waste more time looking for the witness, and letting other classes see us in such a shameful light. That’s all.&quot; and &quot;You are free to interpret things however you wish, but I’m telling you that you’re wrong.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She will move on reasons but never on appeal — the difference between AK&#x27;s point argument, which lands, and Ike&#x27;s or Sudou&#x27;s gratitude, which she calls wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.73, p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ike&#x27;s playful shove on the shoulder ends with her tossing him to the ground and putting him in a headlock: &quot;Don’t touch me. This is your one warning. The next time you try it, I’ll despise you all the way to graduation.&quot; AK&#x27;s note on the technique: &quot;those weren’t the defensive moves of a normal girl. Since I knew that her older brother practiced karate and aikido, she might have learned something, too?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She leaves the second the room turns to teasing her — &quot;Goodbye.&quot; — before anyone can convert her help into belonging.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida is the one who physically keeps her in the room and then the one who asks for her advice; she answers Kushida&#x27;s plan with a judgement, not participation.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> She refuses to let him believe she did it for him, twice, in the same breath in which she hands him the witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 2 4 3  she writes sudou off out loud  and prices the witness ike is the one she interrogates about sudou s actual character   you get along with sudou  don t you  you eat together with him   my  how unfortunate  kushida failed to persuade her    spoken as kushida s approach to sakura collapses in front of the class  ak agrees   horikita was correct  if kushida couldn t do it  then i didn t think that anyone else in our class would be able to  the thesis she alone will say  that a bad witness is a better outcome   she won t testify on your behalf  they ll determine you caused the incident  in the end  class d will be affected by your actions  but we ll be okay  we have testimony that they lied about the violence  it s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident  that way we ll only lose 87 points  and you won t face expulsion  however  we ll shoulder more of the blame than class c will   i don t think self defense is all that helpful in this case    to sudou  after he invokes it again   even your friends don t wish to help you  how unfortunate    and when sudou calls the class useless jerks   what an interesting thing to say  sudou kun  haven t you noticed that everyone is turning on you   i don t show mercy to people who don t attempt to better themselves  he s caused us nothing but harm  and has no redeeming features    ak s silent counter   well  you don t exactly show any mercy even to people ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.88–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike is the one she interrogates about Sudou&#x27;s actual character: &quot;You get along with Sudou, don’t you? You eat together with him.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in…<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have…<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t think self-defense is all that helpful in this case.&quot; — to Sudou, after he invokes it again.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in our class would be able to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have testimony that they lied about the violence. It’s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident. That way we’ll only lose 87 points, and you won’t face expulsion. However, we’ll shoulder more of the blame than Class C will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s tag on that speech: &quot;Horikita relentlessly spoke her thoughts out loud, as if she’d been hiding them deep inside her all this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even your friends don’t wish to help you. How unfortunate,&quot; — and when Sudou calls the class useless jerks: &quot;What an interesting thing to say, Sudou-kun. Haven’t you noticed that everyone is turning on you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t show mercy to people who don’t attempt to better themselves. He’s caused us nothing but harm, and has no redeeming features.&quot; — AK&#x27;s silent counter: &quot;Well, you don’t exactly show any mercy even to people who do attempt such things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to deny that it could happen in 10 years’ time, but I’m looking for things to help me reach Class A right now. If he can’t help us right now, then he’s worthless to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her evidentiary standard, delivered as a dismissal of the whole search: &quot;Considering the circumstances, even if we get Sakura-san’s testimony, I believe it’ll have minimal impact. The school will probably have doubts about a witness just suddenly appearing from Class D.&quot; and &quot;They’ll consider the witness’s testimony along with her possible intentions. They won’t take her word as absolute proof.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The only case that would actually work: &quot;the best and most miraculous situation would be if there was a trusted witness from another class or grade who saw the entire incident from start to finish. There isn’t anyone who fits that description, though,&quot; — AK: &quot;said Horikita with confidence.&quot; and &quot;I thought the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She takes no part in stopping Sudou from hitting Kōenji; the physical intervention is Hirata&#x27;s, and her contribution is the sentence that made him angry enough to need it.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 4  she invites ayanokoji out  and decides on class b she initiates  for the first time in the volume   ayanokouji kun  do you want to head back together    and asks for a ten minute stop on the way   it should only take about 10 minutes  she steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears   i have something i d like to ask you  sakura san    and ak has to physically restrain her from pursuing   i tried to gently restrain horikita  gesturing for her for stop chasing sakura  her first question at the special building is about him  not the case   you ve really changed  haven t you  it s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case  the witness has already been found  and we ve confirmed that there s nothing left to be done  what are you even trying to do   well  your way of thinking isn t relevant to me  ayanokouji kun  so you re free to think whatever you like  also  i appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with    and on being asked whether she just hates hirata and kushida   having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation  her actual objective  once she stops pretending she has none   sudou has many qualities i can t stomach  however  i want to lessen the blame they re placing upon him  the best possible outcome is we ll still have some points  even if class d s image worsens    ak s note   she sounded honest  normally  she wasn t quite so candid   like i said  unless a perfect witness appears  proving sudou kun s innocence will be impossible  if th","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.95–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She initiates, for the first time in the volume: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, do you want to head back together?&quot; — and asks for a ten-minute stop on the way, &quot;It should only take about 10 minutes.&quot; She steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears: &quot;I have something I’d like to ask you, Sakura-san,&quot; — and AK has to physically restrain her from pursuing: &quot;I tried to gently restrain Horikita, gesturing for her for stop chasing Sakura.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and…<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points…<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She absorbs an unasked-for physical check without punishment: after AK&#x27;s hand goes to her forehead she says only &quot;Do you mind? Your hand.&quot; — where minutes earlier she had put Ike in a headlock for touching her shoulder, a contrast AK&#x27;s own line records.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s nothing left to be done. What are you even trying to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and Kushida: &quot;Having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She audits the building for evidence rather than waiting for it — &quot;Looks like there aren’t any here. Too bad,&quot; and, when asked what she means: &quot;Cameras, like the ones in the classrooms. If there were cameras here, we’d have solid evidence. I can’t find any.&quot; — and sets the rule&#x27;s boundary: &quot;If I had to think of places where they wouldn’t be installed, I’d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points, even if Class D’s image worsens.&quot; — AK&#x27;s note: &quot;She sounded honest. Normally, she wasn’t quite so candid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Like I said, unless a perfect witness appears, proving Sudou-kun’s innocence will be impossible. If those Class C students admitted that they lied, I suppose things might turn out fine. Do you think that’s likely?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but think there’s an ulterior motive,&quot; — to Ichinose, uninvited, before any question is answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to talk with someone who is ‘just curious.’ Do what you want.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita tried to put some distance between them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you finished? You heard what you wanted.&quot; — &quot;Horikita spoke sharply and with a sigh, trying to drive Ichinose away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The reversal, in one sentence, after weighing nothing out loud: &quot;Let’s accept her help, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita had made a decision, probably determining that the benefits outweighed the risks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She gives her name first, which AK reads as the act of opening an alliance: &quot;Horikita gave her name candidly, as if doing so approved our cooperative relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the first I’m hearing about it affecting our class points. I’ll have to complain to Chabashira-sensei later,&quot; — AK: &quot;mumbled Horikita, a little disgruntled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She accepts being cast as the threat in his speech to Sakura without argument: &quot;Are you talking about me?&quot; — muttered, then dropped.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hostility on sight, then a partnership in the same afternoon: she is the one who says no twice, the one who says yes, and the one whose name seals it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 4 4 5  she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is she outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look   horikita shot me a look that seemed to say  i don t want to do it  give her yours  the one moment of her own body language he gets to see  and she names it herself   why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger     to hide my pounding heart  or something  her only environmental protest in the volume  delivered to a stranger   a school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst    ichinose laughs anyway   ha ha ha  that s probably true  you re pretty interesting  she declines a spare key to his room before being offered one  and calls the visit itself a failing   for your room  ike kun asked earlier if i wanted one  i refused     after all  it s rare for me to visit your room  ayanokouji kun  besides  coming here is a shameful act in itself  a disgrace  understand    ak   i wasn t hurt at all  i definitely wasn t thinking anything like  wow  that was unexpectedly harsh  her agenda for the visit  stated as two problems   ayanokouji kun  i want to hear your thoughts on sudou kun s case once again  also  i find kushida san s actions a bit concerning   impossible  the very person in question didn t recognize what was happening  i m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class  frankly  i still think it would have been better to abandon him  the pedago","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.108–113<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look: &quot;Horikita shot me a look that seemed to say, I don’t want to do it. Give her yours.&quot; The one moment of her own body language he gets to see, and she names it herself: “Why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger?” / “To hide my pounding heart. Or something.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room…<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her agenda for the visit, stated as two problems: “Ayanokouji-kun, I want to hear your thoughts on Sudou-kun’s case once again. Also, I find Kushida-san’s actions a bit concerning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s probably true. You’re pretty interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room, Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, coming here is a shameful act in itself. A disgrace. Understand?” — AK: &quot;I wasn’t hurt at all. I definitely wasn’t thinking anything like, Wow, that was unexpectedly harsh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible. The very person in question didn’t recognize what was happening. I’m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class. Frankly, I still think it would have been better to abandon him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The pedagogical claim she makes for not saving him: “That was different. Even if we managed to miraculously prove his innocence, do you think he’ll mature? Saving him might have the opposite effect.” — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Her defiant glare seemed to say, Do you understand my point?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She turns his own reasoning back on him in real time: “Knowing Sudou’s flawed personality, you realized from the very beginning how difficult it would be to prove his innocence, didn’t you? That way, it’s easier to think he’d be better off accepting his punishment. Especially better for those who hate him.” — AK&#x27;s record of being caught: &quot;I felt like I’d been backed against a wall, unable to run. If I tried to forcefully deny, she would just dig deeper.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on the rest of Class D, delivered as mercilessly as AK notes: “Kushida-san and Ike-kun and the others haven’t noticed at all, it seems. They simply believe in Sudou-kun, and want to save him from the lie for his sake and our class’s sake. They don’t understand the urgency of the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A little bit? So she realized it by herself, then?” and “You told her, didn’t you?” — AK: &quot;She cornered me with her words. It was like being interrogated. A little scary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The accusation that he engineered the midterm operations: “You came up with the idea of getting the old test questions, and purchasing exam points. I can’t say I’m surprised. You do seem quite cunning at times, but…I’m dissatisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her full description of him, the volume&#x27;s closest attempt at a characterisation of Ayanokōji by another student: “Honestly, there’s so much about you that I don’t understand. You’re a mystery. You’re the most difficult person to predict in our class. You’re versatile, yet you often idle your time away. You never seem to stay still. It’s as though you cannot be categorized.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then the sentence he cannot deflect: “I guess what I should say is that you’re just blending in and hiding your true talents. You’re hiding in plain sight. You disgust me more than anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She does not actually know what he did, and stops at a feeling: &quot;I see. I wondered if being called out like that was normal. It seemed I’d taken the bait and gotten caught in Horikita’s trap. A small failure on my part.&quot; — AK&#x27;s own accounting of the conversation&#x27;s cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her Kōenji assessment, offered as the counter-example to his mysteriousness: “He’s surprisingly easy to understand. He studies well, is athletic, and gets excellent grades. His personality is the problem. In the end, I can easily categorize and summarize his behavioral problems in only a few words: he’s self-centered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is candid only in private and only with one person; the entire volume&#x27;s worth of her actual analysis of Class D — Sudou, Kushida, Ayanokōji, Kōenji — is delivered in his room in one sitting, and none of it survives as anything but privately held when she re-enters a classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK&#x27;s own note on the setting, which should not be over-read: &quot;I wondered why I felt a little nervous being alone with Horikita behind closed doors.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK&#x27;s projection of her, the chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;At this rate, when she reached adulthood, she’d probably become a teacher like Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 4  4 6 4 8  named by everyone  present nowhere  kushida  relaying her conclusion to the one person horikita will not speak to directly   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  kushida s summary of her  offered as the standing question of the class   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in class d  kushida s probe about her   but doesn t she behave normally with you  ayanokouji kun  how ayanokoji describes her to a third party  which is the only version of her kushida receives   when i think of my relationship with horikita  it s like there s a wall between us  or perhaps i should say that s the extent of our relationship  if you understand what i m getting at","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.118–130<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida, relaying her conclusion to the one person Horikita will not speak to directly: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me…<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Kushida&#x27;s probe about her: &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s roster of who is actually carrying Class D, in his own words: &quot;Actually, the ones who had to work especially hard were Horikita, Hirata, and Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The first name in his private list of students wrongly sorted into Class D: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> How Ayanokōji describes her to a third party, which is the only version of her Kushida receives: &quot;When I think of my relationship with Horikita, it’s like there’s a wall between us. Or perhaps I should say that’s the extent of our relationship, if you understand what I’m getting at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His withheld verdict on her exceptionalism, kept off the phone: &quot;Horikita wasn’t special. She belonged to a unique class of people. I kept quiet, though, afraid that if I badmouthed her she’d find out about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan that would place her beside the witness is cancelled before it is proposed, by the person organising the errand: &quot;While taking Horikita along would probably be the best option, it was delusional to think that Horikita and Kushida would spend their day off together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of this is secondhand. The second half of Chapter 4 contains no Horikita scene; her last appearance is alone with Ayanokōji in his room, and the class&#x27;s entire summer-facing strategy is discussed without her in the room where it is decided.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 1  the face she does not intend to make morning  the classroom  she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls  an icy voice   did you spend your day off with kushida san   really  i didn t intend to make any kind of face  i should look the same as i always do  however  i will say that i admire how freely you ve been moving  when i ask you for help  you re often reluctant  but when kushida san asks you  you accept readily  i was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning, the classroom; she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls &quot;an icy voice&quot;.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Did you spend your day off with Kushida-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks…<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks you, you accept readily. I was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The denial is contradicted on the page: &quot;I looked over at my neighbor, and saw an expression on Horikita’s face that I’d never glimpsed before.&quot; then &quot;She did not remotely look calm and discreet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida reads the same face as exclusion; the narrator refuses that reading and then concedes a realization he cannot name.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 2 5 3  she takes the seats and refuses the optimism at lunch she eats  her bread in silence  while the others argue   well  naturally that was the result  it s to be expected   now then  kushida san  it would be best for ayanokouji kun and me to sit in on the deliberation  i fully understand you supporting sakura san  however  if it comes to a debate  then that s a different story   don t bring your dirty face so close to me   i can t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven  although you ve gained evidence that works in your favor  you re still in a very disadvantageous situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.165–167<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At lunch she eats &quot;her bread in silence&quot; while the others argue.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, naturally that was the result. It’s to be expected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Now then, Kushida-san. It would be best for Ayanokouji-kun and me to sit in on the deliberation. I fully understand you supporting Sakura-san. However, if it comes to a debate, then that’s a different story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t bring your dirty face so close to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She takes the two observer places Kushida asked for, and Sakura is left agreeing to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven. Although you’ve gained evidence that works in your favor, you’re still in a very disadvantageous situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 4  the elevator  and a question she answers herself the elevator  she is inside with shopping bags  the thirteenth floor button lit  he presses eleven   what  you re not getting on   i was out shopping  did you not see   this isn t the tenth floor  is that okay   for someone who dislikes trouble  you ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case  or perhaps you have ulterior motives   you re going to meet with sakura san  aren t you   well  i suppose where you go is none of my business","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.170–171<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The elevator: she is inside with shopping bags, the thirteenth-floor button lit; he presses eleven.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What? You’re not getting on?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was out shopping. Did you not see?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This isn’t the tenth floor. Is that okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For someone who dislikes trouble, you’ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case. Or perhaps you have ulterior motives?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re going to meet with Sakura-san, aren’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well. I suppose where you go is none of my business.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the question, then withdraws it, without waiting for the answer he does not give.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6 open  the hearing she is not ready for class d s room  ten minutes before the hearing  sudo asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him  outside the faculty room  chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in  horikita freezes at the words   have you prepared for this  sudou kun   don t do anything selfish  actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do  yes   i ll go  i m fine","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–192<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room, ten minutes before the hearing; Sudō asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him. Outside the faculty room, Chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in; Horikita freezes at the words.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Have you prepared for this, Sudou-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t do anything selfish. Actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do, yes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll go. I’m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator reads the exchange as habitual combat without hatred: Sudō &quot;would’ve absolutely refused her help&quot; if he truly resented her.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s send-off — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — is the only encouragement Horikita receives before the hearing, and she does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The glance she gives the narrator is read as a request not to worry on her account.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 1  frozen  then roused  then cross examining   hyah   w wait  s stop  stop   tch   excuse me  may i ask a question   earlier  you said that sudou kun called you over to the special building  but who exactly did sudou call  and why   please answer   so then  why exactly were you in the special building  ishizaki kun  you re not on the basketball team  so you have no connection to this case  i d think your presence there would be rather odd   so in other words  you felt the situation might turn violent   i see  so you brought along ishizaki kun as your bodyguard  since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting  just in case there was an emergency   i do have some knowledge of martial arts  if only to a certain extent  i understand that when you re fighting against multiple enemies  victory becomes exponentially more difficult  so i don t understand how you were defeated so handily  how the fight could be so one sided  when you had a skilled fighter like ishizaki kun with you   the primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the  energy  between opponents  in the event that you don t have any intention of fighting  or that you re nonviolent  the probability that you ll be hurt should be very low  especially when there are three of you   it s true that sudou injured the other students  however  class c started the fight  there is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–200<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hyah?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;W-wait. S-stop, stop!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tch…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her brother’s presence undoes her before testimony begins: &quot;Horikita —Horikita the younger sister, I mean—couldn’t hide her trembling,&quot; and the narrator concludes their kinship makes the room &quot;extremely disadvantageous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She is physically roused by the narrator’s tickling and returns to the room glaring &quot;with startling intensity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Excuse me. May I ask a question?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Earlier, you said that Sudou-kun called you over to the special building. But who exactly did Sudou call, and why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please answer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then, why exactly were you in the special building, Ishizaki-kun? You’re not on the basketball team, so you have no connection to this case. I’d think your presence there would be rather odd.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So in other words, you felt the situation might turn violent?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So you brought along Ishizaki-kun as your bodyguard, since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting. Just in case there was an emergency.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I do have some knowledge of martial arts, if only to a certain extent. I understand that when you’re fighting against multiple enemies, victory becomes exponentially more difficult. So I don’t understand how you were defeated so handily, how the fight could be so one-sided, when you had a skilled fighter like Ishizaki-kun with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the ‘energy’ between opponents. In the event that you don’t have any intention of fighting, or that you’re nonviolent, the probability that you’ll be hurt should be very low. Especially when there are three of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her cross-examination turns the witness list into a contradiction: if Ishizaki came as a bodyguard because Sudō was reputed violent, a rehearsed nonviolent group should not have been beaten so one-sidedly.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator credits the method as &quot;very objective, grounded in evidence, rules, and her own logic,&quot; and notes Komiya answers it with his actual injuries rather than with argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s true that Sudou injured the other students. However, Class C started the fight. There is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 1  the answer to the false witness charge   that is not the case  it is certainly true that sakura san is not good at speaking before others  however  it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today  otherwise  she most likely would not  even if we d asked her  don t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly  we would have found a replacement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.203<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not…<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not, even if we’d asked her. Don’t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly, we would have found a replacement?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami answers it by claiming the choice of a poor speaker is itself the staging: &quot;it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 1  the false concession  then the refusal   i understand   i think that sudou  who caused the incident  has a problem  he doesn t ever stop to consider his actions  which inconveniences everyone around him  he has a history of getting in fights  he s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him  in the event of an uproar such as this  well  it should be obvious who caused it   you need to understand  sudou  your attitude caused all of this   this is why i wasn t motivated at all to help sudou kun in the beginning  i knew that even if i forced myself to lend a hand  he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again   he should reflect on his actions  however  not in this particular case  when i say he should reflect  i mean that he should look back on his past actions  in regards to this particular incident  however  i don t think sudou kun did anything wrong  this was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance  i m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by class c  i have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat   if you did not understand  i will say it once again  we claim that sudou kun is completely innocent  therefore  we cannot accept his suspension from school  even for just one day   sudou kun is the victim  just as the witness testified  please do not make any errors in your judgment   would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.207–209<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and…<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You need to understand, Sudou. Your attitude caused all of this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him. In the event of an uproar such as this, well, it should be obvious who caused it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is why I wasn’t motivated at all to help Sudou-kun in the beginning. I knew that even if I forced myself to lend a hand, he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The closing statement is a trap: she lets Sakagami treat it as surrender, then refuses to sit, and the silence is what gives her the floor back.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He should reflect on his actions. However, not in this particular case. When I say he should reflect, I mean that he should look back on his past actions. In regards to this particular incident, however, I don’t think Sudou-kun did anything wrong. This was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance. I’m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by Class C. I have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you did not understand, I will say it once again. We claim that Sudou-kun is completely innocent. Therefore, we cannot accept his suspension from school, even for just one day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun is the victim, just as the witness testified. Please do not make any errors in your judgment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reversal is made for Sakura’s sake as much as Sudō’s: the narrator guesses she &quot;had to be brave in front of Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line answering the president’s question to Class D — &quot;I haven’t lied. Everything we’ve said has been the truth.&quot; — is untagged in the translation; it is recorded as Class D’s answer, not attributed to her by name on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 1  what she says to sakura on the way out   i won t give up  i will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end   i have no intention of losing  well then  i must excuse myself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won’t give up. I will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have no intention of losing. Well then, I must excuse myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves immediately after the promise rather than staying to comfort Sakura, and the chapter reads the haste as strategy, not coldness.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 2  the request she makes of class b   i sincerely appreciate the offer  but it s not necessary   we cannot get sudou acquitted  even if a new witness were to come from class a or b  it would be impossible  however there is something i would like you to prepare for us  it is the only possible solution   i understand that i m in no position to ask this   the burden i d be placing upon you is exceptionally great  but   you re certainly right about that  well then  if i can convince you  will you cooperate with us   you should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy   just before the deliberation ended  only by chance  though   don t worry about that part  i ve confirmed it   if you ask the professor to assist us  it should be good  i ll talk to him   sure  i promise   well then  ayanokouji kun  there s something i d like you to help me with   helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time consuming","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.216–218<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I sincerely appreciate the offer, but it’s not necessary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We cannot get Sudou acquitted. Even if a new witness were to come from Class A or B, it would be impossible. However…there is something I would like you to prepare for us. It is the only possible solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I understand that I’m in no position to ask this,&quot; &quot;The burden I’d be placing upon you is exceptionally great. But—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re certainly right about that. Well then, if I can convince you, will you cooperate with us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just before the deliberation ended. Only by chance, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t worry about that part. I’ve confirmed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you ask the Professor to assist us, it should be good. I’ll talk to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sure. I promise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, Ayanokouji-kun. There’s something I’d like you to help me with.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time-consuming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She has a plan before the hearing ends and has already verified that its material exists by the time she explains it in the entranceway.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan requires a lie from a person who hates lying; Horikita acknowledges the burden instead of softening it, and Ichinose supplies the justification herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 6  6 2  the debt she collects   i ll forgive you for touching me this time  however  next time i ll pay you back double","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.218<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll forgive you for touching me this time. However, next time I’ll pay you back double.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She answers the hearing’s tickling with a blow to the narrator’s side that drops him into the corner.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter runs her from paralysis to leadership and closes the account with the blow: she accepts his intervention in the hearing and prices it immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 0 7 1  waiting on the path  judging the change   good morning  ayanokouji kun   yes  i was waiting for you   are you an idiot   i was thinking maybe i made a mistake  the wrong choice   if sudou kun is penalized for this  it ll be my responsibility   the truth is that we re gambling  i m a little anxious of the outcome  are you okay   nothing  after we settle this case   what s with her   people don t change so easily  trying to change yourself is virtually impossible   as long as she doesn t overdo it  i think it ll be fine   if she tries to do what isn t possible for someone like her yet  she ll just set herself up to fail   do you want to die for good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.220–223<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. I was waiting for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you an idiot?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was thinking…maybe I made a mistake. The wrong choice…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Sudou-kun is penalized for this, it’ll be my responsibility.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The truth is that we’re gambling. I’m a little anxious of the outcome. Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing. After we settle this case,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s with her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;People don’t change so easily. Trying to change yourself is virtually impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The page calls it a &quot;brief but realistic statement&quot; that shattered the image Ayanokōji had built.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as she doesn’t overdo it, I think it’ll be fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If she tries to do what isn’t possible for someone like her yet, she’ll just set herself up to fail.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The warning lands with &quot;a mysterious yet convincing power,&quot; almost as if she were speaking from experience.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you want to die for good?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 5  the retrial  from her side she and sudo arrive ten minutes before deliberation  tachibana is already in the room  and neither her brother nor class c has come in yet  the chapter turns to her first person here   i feel the same as ever  the line she has committed to   i d declared that sudou was completely innocent  after all  if my strategy failed  it would be for nothing   reconciliation was another name for defeat  on a failed strategy   it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other   even though i should have understood it  i felt attacked   i was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling  nervousness  and dizziness  but i couldn t repeat yesterday s mistakes   he s not participating   well  even if he s not here  the results will be the same  her read on chabashira s puzzlement   i had the gut feeling that what chabashira sensei was seeing was the evidence of ayanokouji kun s involvement   this was a battle between truth and lies  we could bandy about ideas  but there could only be one solution","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.242–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Sudō arrive ten minutes before deliberation; Tachibana is already in the room, and neither her brother nor Class C has come in yet. The chapter turns to her first person here.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I feel the same as ever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;He’s not participating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, even if he’s not here, the results will be the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The line she has committed to: &quot;I’d declared that Sudou was completely innocent, after all. If my strategy failed, it would be for nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Reconciliation was another name for defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On a failed strategy: &quot;it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the doors open for her brother she turns her eyes away from him and faces the opponents who matter today.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even though I should have understood it, I felt attacked.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling, nervousness, and dizziness. But I couldn’t repeat yesterday’s mistakes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Her read on Chabashira’s puzzlement: &quot;I had the gut feeling that what Chabashira-sensei was seeing was the evidence of Ayanokouji-kun’s involvement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;This was a battle between truth and lies. We could bandy about ideas, but there could only be one solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 5  the withdrawal she did not have to ask for   it wasn t just me  everyone else noticed that this situation was strange   it seemed that ayanokouji kun and ichinose san had handled things quite well  i tried to act calm and collected  without letting my relief show   shut up   if the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers  this was what we d been working toward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.244–245<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;It wasn’t just me. Everyone else noticed that this situation was strange.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;It seemed that Ayanokouji-kun and Ichinose-san had handled things quite well. I tried to act calm and collected, without letting my relief show.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Shut up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She grabs Sudō’s arm to stop his question and pulls him down into his seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers. This was what we’d been working toward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The regulations line that announces a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 5  the verdict  and chabashira s lecture to sudo   you will no longer face suspension  the school will not consider you a problem child  you will be able to participate in club activities from today onward  right   no  i don t    asked whether sudo will become a model student  however sudou kun certainly made some progress today  he admitted he was at fault  so i m sure that he ll grow more tomorrow   no  i ve already abandoned him  i just won t allow him to run loose anymore  on his exit for club practice   he was not remorseful  he was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon  he was a nuisance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–248<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You will no longer face suspension. The school will not consider you a problem child. You will be able to participate in club activities from today onward. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, I don’t.&quot; — asked whether Sudō will become a model student<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;However…Sudou-kun certainly made some progress today. He admitted he was at fault. So I’m sure that he’ll grow more tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She notes that Kushida-san and Hirata-kun’s actions in the hearing &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I’ve already abandoned him. I just won’t allow him to run loose anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On his exit for club practice: &quot;He was not remorseful. He was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon. He was a nuisance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She stays behind at Chabashira’s request once her brother and Tachibana are sent out.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 5  the private lesson about ayanokoji   what do you mean   why do you care about that   i ll leave that to your imagination   we d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner   i don t want to admit this  but ayanokouji kun might have something exceptional to him   is that surprising  you were the one who first put me together with ayanokouji kun  chabashira sensei  you did it because you couldn t overlook ayanokouji kun s potential  right   though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot  for some mysterious reason   yes  he was truly incomprehensible  i could not find meaning in such behavior   i don t intend to admit that i have a defect  but i do understand   we ve already established it  he already knows what his own defect is   he  dislikes trouble   no  it s because he said it himself   had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well   that unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort   chabashira sensei  do you really understand what about him can be considered defective   why was chabashira sensei telling me such things","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.248–251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What do you mean?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why do you care about that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ll leave that to your imagination.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;We’d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to admit this, but Ayanokouji-kun…might have something exceptional to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that surprising? You were the one who first put me together with Ayanokouji-kun, Chabashira-sensei. You did it because you couldn’t overlook Ayanokouji-kun’s potential, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot, for some mysterious reason.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Yes, he was truly incomprehensible. I could not find meaning in such behavior.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to admit that I have a defect. But I do understand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’ve already established it. He already knows what his own defect is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He ‘dislikes trouble,’&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Answering with confidence, she still feels &quot;a strange sense of discomfort that I couldn’t explain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No… It’s because he said it himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;That unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei, do you really understand what about him can be considered defective?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Why was Chabashira-sensei telling me such things?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The session ends with Chabashira saying nothing more and Horikita carrying the questions out of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.248–251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\">→ After: Ch.7 §7.6: the puppet question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 7  7 6  the puppet question   you d already know  right   hey  ayanokouji kun  am i just your puppet   ayanokouji kun  you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms  next  you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras  then  you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence  so that we could parse the truth from lies  when i look back on it now  that s all i can think of   who are you    thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case  just coincidence   and you are    to the black haired boy who stops in front of them  wait  we re not done talking  ayanokouji kun   you promised  right  you promised you d help me reach class a   that s not what i meant  i want to know what you re thinking   if you really hated drawing attention  you wouldn t make all this effort to get involved  you say you re someone who  dislikes trouble  after all  yet you act all evasive and non committal even while you help me  why","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 §7.6: the puppet question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.253–255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You’d already know, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hey, Ayanokouji-kun. Am I just your puppet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false…<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence, so that we could parse the truth from lies… When I look back on it now, that’s all I can think of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who are you?&quot; — thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case &quot;just coincidence&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And you are?&quot; — to the black-haired boy who stops in front of them<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wait. We’re not done talking, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You promised, right? You promised you’d help me reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not what I meant. I want to know what you’re thinking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you really hated drawing attention, you wouldn’t make all this effort to get involved. You say you’re someone who ‘dislikes trouble,’ after all. Yet you act all evasive and non-committal even while you help me. Why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter ends with her accusation of being steered and his evasion, unanswered.<span class=\"pg\">p.253–255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">← Before: Ch.7 §7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 0  she comes down from the ship wrong deck of the liner at disembark call  class d waits in the heat   i was just reading a book in my room  for whom the bell tolls  you wouldn t know it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.22–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner at disembark call; Class D waits in the heat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was just reading a book in my room. For Whom the Bell Tolls. You wouldn’t know it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Even Horikita, normally so meticulous, was concerned about her appearance. Right now, though, her hair was disheveled.&quot; — and she rubs her arms as if cold.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her stated excuse for locking herself away doesn&#x27;t cover what Ayanokōji saw; the chapter leaves the gap open.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 1  she asks the questions that price the test class d s first rules huddle on the beach after mashima s announcement   in the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points  what would happen    the question that establishes the floor at zero   i m the same as the others  i ve never lived in such an environment before  so i can t really make any predictions  what an unpleasant test    her first open admission that academics don t transfer here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D&#x27;s first rules huddle on the beach after Mashima&#x27;s announcement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points, what would happen?” — the question that establishes the floor at zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m the same as the others. I’ve never lived in such an environment before, so I can’t really make any predictions… What an unpleasant test.” — her first open admission that academics don&#x27;t transfer here.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stands beside Ayanokōji watching Hirata fail to decide: &quot;Class D has no leadership, which worries me. Besides, Hirata’s a pushover. He can’t even make one decision, can he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks him to take her side on endurance; he agrees; Classes A and B are already moving into the forest while C and D still can&#x27;t start.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  she admits the isolation  and blocks the probe walking from beach to forest  she trails the group alone   to be honest  i m depressed  these kinds of things just aren t for me  life on an island seems primitive  and worst of all  i can t be alone   it doesn t feel good to have someone pry into your past    and names chabashira as the leak   chabashira sensei leaked the information  don t misunderstand me  all right  besides  we re still not friends  don t forget that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“To be honest, I’m depressed. These kinds of things just aren’t for me. Life on an island seems primitive, and worst of all, I can’t be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It doesn’t feel good to have someone pry into your past” — and names Chabashira as the leak: “Chabashira-sensei leaked the information. Don’t misunderstand me. All right? Besides, we’re still not friends. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes the classroom verdict against her own tools: &quot;This test will likely fall outside of my academic abilities. I’d determined that Ike-kun and Sudou-kun would be hindrances, but they took the initiative to go out searching. I wasn’t able to do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ends the exchange on her own terms before he can go deeper.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 4  the leader s card  and the favour she can t do herself the circle that picks class d s spot leader   i understand  i accept    after sudou tries to take the role to spare her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The circle that picks Class D&#x27;s spot-leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand. I accept.” — after Sudou tries to take the role to spare her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida nominates her as the responsible choice; she accepts without visible surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Becomes Class D&#x27;s designated leader; Hirata files her name with Chabashira and the card is handed over; the class touches the device together to hide who holds it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His defence of her wishes is the trigger that makes her take the role rather than dodge it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delegates the Ike problem — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it. Can I count on you?&quot; — then delivers the standard put-down: “I suppose it must be relaxing to be unreliable and underachieving. … Isn’t it, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s closing read of her: alone she is &quot;amazing…but only alone&quot;; the school &quot;had made her isolated life impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5    2 8  she refuses the assistantship  and votes last","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.73–74, p.92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On becoming Hirata&#x27;s assistant: “Me, his assistant? Don’t joke around. I’d rather dance with a mongoose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Names her own usable condition — &quot;If there were a clear enemy and a goal, I might be of…use&quot; — and admits she still can&#x27;t decide how far the class should spend.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises her hand for river water last, with Ayanokōji, after the whole class has already committed.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 1  called out of the tent summoned from the girls  tent after the class c provocation  the cloth moves  and she steps out   the cheap provocation coming from class c  yes  i heard   i don t want to move too much  since i m the leader  if i stand out too much  we ll be in a bad spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.106–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned from the girls&#x27; tent after the Class C provocation; the cloth moves, and she steps out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The cheap provocation coming from Class C? Yes, I heard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don&#x27;t want to move too much. Since I&#x27;m the leader, if I stand out too much, we&#x27;ll be in a bad spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes she cannot stay hidden — the president&#x27;s younger sister, seen watching Ryūen and Ichinose: “You&#x27;re right. I suppose I can&#x27;t say what&#x27;s correct. Fine. I&#x27;m rather concerned about the state of the other classes. Let&#x27;s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes his read that hiding will not change anything and sets out with him for the Class C beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 2  the confrontation on the beach the class c beach spectacle  she cannot believe what she is looking at   no way  all this stuff  is it even possible   if the person on top is incompetent  those below him will suffer  this is pitiful   we re trying to warn you  you re an idiot   there is one more piece of business  you know ibuki  of course   you used up all your points on the first day  didn t you   see you later  suzune   i don t know where exactly you found that out  but do not call me by my first name so casually","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–114<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach spectacle; she cannot believe what she is looking at.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No way… All this stuff… Is it even possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If the person on top is incompetent, those below him will suffer. This is pitiful,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We&#x27;re trying to warn you. You&#x27;re an idiot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Walks up to his chair with Ayanokōji and holds the confrontation to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the line untagged; his reply is thrown back at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Asks who hit Ibuki roundabout — “Her face is swollen. Who did that to her?” — and gets the admission of a light punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is one more piece of business. You know Ibuki, of course?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You…used up all your points on the first day, didn&#x27;t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know where exactly you found that out, but do not call me by my first name so casually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also untagged; she is the one addressed by the first-name call.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 3  the walk back  and class b s camp walking inland from the class c shore  she is still arguing over ryuen s spending when the visit to class b s camp begins   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   i was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship  like last time   yeah  there s a lot to make us uneasy right now  but we have to try and make it through   i was thinking that we should talk about that  too  if we didn t have to be on guard with even one class  we d really appreciate it  as long as you don t mind  ichinose san  i d like you to accept the proposal   this class has fallen in line far better than i could have imagined  i suppose that s because you re the one taking command  right   no  we do have a boy named hirata  though  everyone in class clusters around him   ichinose san  i m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions  but we want to confirm class a s status  can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp  even something you know about the area might really help   secretive  what kind of measures has class a taken   you can t use any sly tricks in this test  ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points  they might be having fun right now  but they re going to regret it later   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long   ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking inland from the Class C shore, she is still arguing over Ryūen&#x27;s spending when the visit to Class B&#x27;s camp begins.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship, like last time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. There’s a lot to make us uneasy right now, but we have to try and make it through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rejects the zero-points route on principle: points are to be won back, not written off.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Arrives as a visitor with Ayanokōji and declines the hammock offer, so Ichinose sits instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Listens through the whole tour — well, water shower, toilet, vinyl, heat — without interrupting.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Afterward lays out Class D&#x27;s situation completely, holding nothing back in the interest of fairness.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was thinking that we should talk about that, too. If we didn’t have to be on guard with even one class, we’d really appreciate it. As long as you don’t mind, Ichinose-san, I’d like you to accept the proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; she is the one addressing Ichinose by name, and Ichinose&#x27;s proposal and reply are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This class has fallen in line far better than I could have imagined. I suppose that’s because you’re the one taking command, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges Class B by its order: every student carrying out a role, and doing the duty happily, with nobody trying to skip out.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. We do have a boy named Hirata, though. Everyone in class clusters around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him as the one Class D gathers around, then changes the topic.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose-san. I’m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions, but we want to confirm Class A’s status. Can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp? Even something you know about the area might really help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Secretive? What kind of measures has Class A taken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t use any sly tricks in this test. Ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points. They might be having fun right now, but they’re going to regret it later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; the narration that follows anchors the withheld withdrawal plan on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In general, I think we’re all on the same page, but they’re further ahead. I can’t deny it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Says it as a declaration of defeat: the distance between D and B is not only a matter of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 4  talking past class a at the cave she and ayanokoji walk up to the class a cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything   what are you planning  we gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves   we came to snoop  you have a problem   i mean  i would ve thought that since you re in class a you d be clever  but   well  rather than clever  i d say you re underhanded  what cowardly methods   i m horikita  from class d   stupid  huh  in that case  there s no harm in us seeing what s inside  right  or does that make you feel uncomfortable   so it s not a problem if we look  you re in the way   we re just going to look inside  that itself isn t a violation of the rules  right   oh  so you occupy this place  i didn t know that  is there a device inside   well  there definitely aren t any rules that say we can t go into the cave  it s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it s being occupied  but that s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything  we should have the right to look inside  or at least to verify if there s equipment  right  if we couldn t do that  then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot  that s not what this test is about   you re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot  the rules don t protect such actions   well  fine  i look forward to seeing the results  and class a s abilities","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Ayanokōji walk up to the Class A cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you planning? We gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We came to snoop. You have a problem?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I mean, I would’ve thought that since you’re in Class A you’d be clever, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The approach dialogue is untagged; the question-and-answer chain, and the question tagged to her at the end of it, put these on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Switches into a deliberate provocation — the narration calls it a daring switch flipped in her brain.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, rather than clever, I’d say you’re underhanded. What cowardly methods.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stupid, huh? In that case, there’s no harm in us seeing what’s inside, right? Or does that make you feel uncomfortable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s not a problem if we look? You’re in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re just going to look inside. That itself isn’t a violation of the rules, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? So you occupy this place. I didn’t know that. Is there a device inside?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Provokes him on purpose and talks past every block he puts up.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there definitely aren’t any rules that say we can’t go into the cave. It’s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it’s being occupied, but that’s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything. We should have the right to look inside, or at least to verify if there’s equipment, right? If we couldn’t do that, then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot. That’s not what this test is about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The monopoly argument: occupation bars use, not looking, and a spot that nobody may inspect could be seized by anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot. The rules don’t protect such actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both p.128 lines are untagged; the second is answered by Katsuragi conceding the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Matched and stopped by his unspoken-rule argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fine. I look forward to seeing the results, and Class A’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Leaves with the wind knocked out of her; without Katsuragi&#x27;s arrival she would have gone through the vinyl.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her mutters “W-wait.” and “Ugh, what an unintelligible, half-assed answer.” are untagged; the second answers his own admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"ch 5  5 2  the invitation at her desk closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour s side  sudou s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings   why   how stupid  it doesn t matter at all that it s summer vacation  why are you even inviting me out in the first place","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2: the invitation at her desk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Closing ceremonies at her desk neighbour’s side; Sudou’s summer invitation arrives the moment the bell rings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How stupid. It doesn’t matter at all that it’s summer vacation. Why are you even inviting me out in the first place?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Refuses him flatly, then finishes getting ready and leaves the classroom without another word while he is still mid-pitch.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The call that opens the exchange and the sign-off at the end are untagged between the three of them; both are left with the chapter’s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
